  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A pair of arrays AAA and BBB, both of length NNN, are called perfect if it is possible to form an array CCC of length NNN satisfying the following conditions:\n\n\nCi=AiC_i = A_iCi​=Ai​ or Ci=BiC_i = B_iCi​=Bi​ for each 1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N\nCi&lt;Ci+1C_i &lt; C_{i + 1}Ci​&lt;Ci+1​ for each 1≤i&lt;N1 \\le i &lt; N1≤i&lt;N\nYou are given 222 arrays AAA and BBB of length NNN. It is guaranteed that each element from 111 to 2⋅N2 \\cdot N2⋅N either occurs once in AAA or occurs once in BBB.\n\nFind how many pairs LLL and RRR exist such that:\n\n\n1≤L≤R≤N1 \\le L \\le R \\le N1≤L≤R≤N\nThe pair of arrays A[L,R]A[L, R]A[L,R] and B[L,R]B[L, R]B[L,R] are perfect.\nHere, A[L,R]A[L, R]A[L,R] represents the subrange [AL,AL+1,…,AR][A_L, A_{L + 1}, \\ldots, A_R][AL​,AL+1​,…,AR​] of the array AAA.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer NNN - the size of the arrays.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe third line contains NNN integers - B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of LLL and RRR, such that corresponding subranges in AAA and BBB are perfect.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai,Bi≤2⋅N1 \\le A_i, B_i \\le 2 \\cdot N1≤Ai​,Bi​≤2⋅N",
      "Ai≠Aj,Bi≠BjA_i \\ne A_j, B_i \\ne B_jAi​=Aj​,Bi​=Bj​ for any 1≤i&lt;j≤N1 \\le i \\lt j \\le N1≤i&lt;j≤N",
      "Ai≠BjA_i \\ne B_jAi​=Bj​ for any 1≤i,j≤N1 \\le i, j \\le N1≤i,j≤N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
